<title>UK: UKs Blair sees early signs of better BSE deal.</title>
<headline>UKs Blair sees early signs of better BSE deal.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prime Minister Tony Blair said on Wednesday there were early signs that his government would be able to negotiate &quot;a far better deal&quot; to end the mad cow crisis than the Conservative administration could have got.</p>
<p>Speaking at the first session of Prime Minister's question time since the election, Blair said his government had inherited &quot;a quite appalling situation&quot; in relation to Bovine Spongiform Encephalopathy.</p>
<p>&quot;The way that these negotiations (with the EU to lift the ban on beef exports) were handled were a disgrace,&quot; Blair said.</p>
<p>&quot;It will take time to sort it out, but I think that the early indications are that we are able to get a far better deal than the previous government,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7767</p>
